IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- notifying the Commissioner of a
-- retrenchment: s 96A, with what follows from a failure to comply (s 101(3),
-- s 102(5), ss 126A(aa), 126B(1)(aa), 126C(6), 126D) and who is an
-- "employee" for the purpose (s 2(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from
-- 5 December 2025), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt.
-- Section numbers were taken from the body of the deposit.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0289 (Haziq scenario, event h065): an
-- employer with 40 employees retrenches 12 of them in one exercise -- must it
-- notify the Commissioner, within what time, and with what particulars?
--
-- THE ACT ANSWERS ONLY THE FIRST PART. s 96A makes the duty depend entirely on
-- a notification the Commissioner publishes in the Gazette: which employers,
-- which retrenchments, the time, the form and the particulars are all "as may
-- be specified in the notification". The Act itself states no headcount, no
-- workforce size, no period and no deadline. The notification was not
-- retrieved, so this module takes "a notification applies and covers this
-- retrenchment" as a supplied fact, and reports WHERE each answer is fixed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the content of any Gazette notification under s 96A (thresholds,
-- deadline, form, particulars); the prescribed amounts of administrative
-- penalty and the prescribed periods and procedure under s 126C; s 126B(2)-(4)
-- (contents and payment of a contravention notice); s 126C(1)-(5), (7) and (8)
-- (reconsideration, appeal, enforcement through a District Court, waiver);
-- Government officers declared by the President to be employees (s 2(1)); s 45
-- (no retrenchment benefit under 2 years' continuous service) is already in
-- ea-part4-hours.l4.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- approach. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- s 96A, retrenchment information`

§§ `96A(1) -- what the Commissioner may require, and where each answer is fixed`

-- s 96A(1): "The Commissioner MAY, BY NOTIFICATION IN THE GAZETTE, require any
-- employer, or any employer in a class of employers, to furnish to the
-- Commissioner, AT SUCH TIME AND IN SUCH FORM AS MAY BE SPECIFIED IN THE
-- NOTIFICATION, SUCH INFORMATION on the retrenchment of any employee by the
-- employer AS MAY BE SPECIFIED IN THE NOTIFICATION."
--
-- So every particular of the duty is delegated. The one number the Act does fix
-- in this area is the fine for disobeying a direction under s 126D(2).
DECLARE `Retrenchment reporting matter` IS ONE OF
    `which employers must report`
    `which retrenchments must be reported`
    `the time for reporting`
    `the form of the report`
    `the particulars to be given`
    `the amount of an administrative penalty`
    `the maximum fine for disobeying a direction`

DECLARE `Where it is fixed` IS ONE OF
    `the Act itself`
    `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
    `the amount prescribed under section 126B(1)`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Retrenchment reporting matter`
GIVETH A `Where it is fixed`
DECIDE `where the answer is fixed` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `which employers must report` THEN `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
    WHEN `which retrenchments must be reported` THEN `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
    WHEN `the time for reporting` THEN `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
    WHEN `the form of the report` THEN `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
    WHEN `the particulars to be given` THEN `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
    WHEN `the amount of an administrative penalty` THEN `the amount prescribed under section 126B(1)`
    OTHERWISE `the Act itself`

§§ `2(1) -- whose retrenchment counts`

-- s 2(1): "employee" means "a person who has entered into or works under a
-- contract of service with an employer ... but does not include any of the
-- following: (a) any seafarer; (b) any domestic worker; ... (d) any person
-- belonging to any other class of persons whom the Minister may, by
-- notification in the Gazette, declare not to be employees".
-- s 96A speaks of "the retrenchment of any employee", so the retrenchment of a
-- seafarer or a domestic worker is outside it.
GIVEN `works under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a seafarer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is in a class the Minister has declared not to be employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` IF
        `works under a contract of service`
    AND (NOT `is a seafarer`)
    AND (NOT `is a domestic worker`)
    AND (NOT `is in a class the Minister has declared not to be employees`)

§§ `96A(2) -- the duty, and compliance counted employee by employee`

-- s 96A(2): "Every employer TO WHOM THE NOTIFICATION APPLIES must comply with
-- every requirement in the notification concerning the furnishing to the
-- Commissioner of information on the retrenchment of any employee by the
-- employer."
--
-- The workforce size and the number retrenched are carried as facts so that the
-- cases can show that the Act ITSELF draws no line on either: only the
-- notification can.
DECLARE RetrenchmentFacts HAS
    `a notification under section 96A(1) is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notification applies to the employer or to a class the employer is in` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notification requires information on this retrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of employees the employer has` IS A NUMBER
    `number of employees retrenched` IS A NUMBER
    `number of retrenched employees for whom every requirement was met` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the facts` IS A RetrenchmentFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` IF
        `the facts`'s `a notification under section 96A(1) is in force`
    AND `the facts`'s `the notification applies to the employer or to a class the employer is in`
    AND `the facts`'s `the notification requires information on this retrenchment`
    AND `the facts`'s `number of employees retrenched` GREATER THAN 0

-- s 126B(1)(aa) counts an occasion "concerning the furnishing to the
-- Commissioner of information on the retrenchment of ANY ONE EMPLOYEE", so a
-- failure is counted per retrenched employee.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A RetrenchmentFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the retrenched employees for whom a requirement was not met` IS
    IF `the facts`'s `number of employees retrenched` GREATER THAN `the facts`'s `number of retrenched employees for whom every requirement was met`
    THEN `the facts`'s `number of employees retrenched` MINUS `the facts`'s `number of retrenched employees for whom every requirement was met`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the facts` IS A RetrenchmentFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has complied with section 96A(2)` IF
        (NOT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` `the facts`)
    OR  `the retrenched employees for whom a requirement was not met` `the facts` EQUALS 0

§§ `126A(aa), 126B(1)(aa) -- a civil contravention, penalised per employee`

-- s 126A: "The following contraventions are declared to be civil
-- contraventions ...: (aa) a failure, by an employer to whom a notification
-- under section 96A applies, to comply with any requirement in the notification
-- concerning the furnishing to the Commissioner of information on the
-- retrenchment of any employee by the employer".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A RetrenchmentFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a civil contravention under section 126A(aa)` IF
        `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` `the facts`
    AND `the retrenched employees for whom a requirement was not met` `the facts` GREATER THAN 0

-- s 126B(1): "An authorised officer MAY issue a contravention notice to an
-- employer requiring the employer to pay an administrative penalty of the
-- PRESCRIBED AMOUNT, for -- ... (aa) EACH OCCASION of an alleged failure ...
-- concerning the furnishing to the Commissioner of information on the
-- retrenchment of ANY ONE EMPLOYEE by the employer".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A RetrenchmentFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` IS
    IF `there is a civil contravention under section 126A(aa)` `the facts`
    THEN `the retrenched employees for whom a requirement was not met` `the facts`
    ELSE 0

-- The most the penalties could total if a notice issued for every occasion at
-- the prescribed amount. "May" -- the officer need not; s 126B(3) allows
-- different amounts for different circumstances, and s 126C(8) allows waiver.
-- The amount is a supplied fact: the regulations were not retrieved.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A RetrenchmentFacts
      `the prescribed amount per occasion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most the administrative penalties could total` IS
    `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` `the facts`
        TIMES `the prescribed amount per occasion`

§§ `101(3), 102(5) -- the returns offence and the secrecy rule do not reach it`

-- s 101(3): "Subsections (1) and (2) DO NOT APPLY to any information furnished
-- or required to be furnished under section 96A by an employer on the
-- retrenchment of any employee by the employer." So a failure to report a
-- retrenchment is NOT the s 101(1) offence (fine up to $5,000 or 6 months).
GIVEN `the information is furnished or required under section 96A on a retrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 101(1) and (2) can apply to the information` IF
    NOT `the information is furnished or required under section 96A on a retrenchment`

-- s 102(5): "Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply to any information furnished
-- under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of any employee by the
-- employer." The s 102 bar on publishing returns without consent does not
-- protect retrenchment information.
GIVEN `the information was furnished under section 96A on a retrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 102(1) to (4) can apply to the information` IF
    NOT `the information was furnished under section 96A on a retrenchment`

§§ `126D -- directions, and the offence of disobeying one`

-- s 126D(1): "In lieu of or in addition to giving an employer a contravention
-- notice ..., an authorised officer may -- (a) issue such directions ... to
-- bring the civil contravention to an end; and (b) ... require the employer to
-- take such action ... to remedy, mitigate or eliminate any effects".
-- s 126D(2): "An employer who, WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE, fails to comply with a
-- direction ... shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 6 months or to both."
`the maximum fine for disobeying a section 126D direction` MEANS 5000
`the maximum imprisonment in months for disobeying a section 126D direction` MEANS 6

GIVEN `a direction was given under section 126D(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has committed the section 126D(2) offence` IF
        `a direction was given under section 126D(1)`
    AND `the employer failed to comply with it`
    AND (NOT `the employer had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `126C(6) -- enforcement stayed while the notice is challenged`

-- s 126C(6): enforcement of the penalty "is stayed -- (a) if a request for
-- internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) is made, until after the
-- reconsideration is completed; or (b) if an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or
-- (4) is filed, until after the appeal is completed."
GIVEN `reconsideration was requested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reconsideration is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `enforcement of the administrative penalty is stayed` IF
        (`reconsideration was requested` AND (NOT `the reconsideration is completed`))
    OR  (`an appeal was filed` AND (NOT `the appeal is completed`))
